* s1rcolor.scheme
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* dash translation of Stata's s1rcolor ("s1 reverse color") graph scheme.
*
* Source Stata scheme file : /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s1rcolor.scheme
*                            (Stata #include chain: s2color -> s1color -> s1rcolor;
*                             byte-identical under /Applications/Stata/ado/base)
* Stata version            : StataNow 19.5 (MP), born 12 Aug 2026
* Extracted (UTC)          : 2026-09-19T16:13:55Z
* Translated (UTC)         : 2026-09-19
* Derived from             : test/fixtures/scheme_truth.json, key "s1rcolor",
*                            generated by scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py from
*                            Stata's own scheme-*.scheme and style/*.style files.
*
* Regenerate the fixture and re-check this file whenever Stata is upgraded:
* the values below were true of the Stata version named above and of no other.
*
* Colours are written as RESOLVED #rrggbb hex, not Stata colour names, on
* purpose.  SchemeParser._color() swallows a colour token OptionTranslator
* cannot resolve and substitutes its "#000000" default, so a name outside
* OptionTranslator._COLOR_MAP silently renders the series black.  Hex is
* self-contained and cannot fail that way.
*
* s1rcolor is the reverse-video scheme: the canvas, plot region and legend are
* genuinely black here, and the heading, axis lines and legend border are
* white.  The black backgrounds below are Stata's own resolved values, not the
* unresolvable-token fallback described above.
*
* This file is flat and standalone - no #include.  Stata's s1rcolor inherits
* most of its body from s1color (and s1color from s2color), but the fixture
* records the fully resolved post-include values, so every directive is
* spelled out here.
*
* Property categories dash's SchemeParser reads:
*   color, symbol, linepattern, linewidth, intensity, gsize, graphsize,
*   symbolsize, clockdir, numstyle
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

label "s1 reverse color"

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Background and region colors
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color background      #000000
color plotregion      #000000
color legend          #000000
color legend_line     #ffffff
color major_grid      #505050
color minor_grid      #808080
color heading         #ffffff
color axisline        #ffffff

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Per-plot color cycle (p1-p15)
* s1rcolor resolves p#, p#line, p#bar and p#mark to the same colour: Stata
* sets only "color p1".."color p15" and every stub falls back to it (fixture
* sources: p_line_colors[i] <- "color p{i}", likewise bar and mark).  dash's
* parser follows the same p#stub -> pstub -> p# -> p chain, so only the p#
* cycle is written.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
color p1      #ffff00
color p2      #00ff00
color p3      #0080ff
color p4      #ff00ff
color p5      #ff7f00
color p6      #ff0000
color p7      #add8e6
color p8      #ffe474
color p9      #00ff80
color p10     #c0dcc0
color p11     #ff4500
color p12     #0000ff
color p13     #ff0080
color p14     #6e8e84
color p15     #a0522d

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Line widths (Stata linewidth style names; "medium" is .30 Stata units)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linewidth p           medium
linewidth major_grid  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Fill intensities
* "intensity area" is not set by any Stata base scheme; s1rcolor resolves it
* through the bare "intensity" class default, which is full (alpha 1.0).  It
* is recorded here under the key dash's parser actually reads.
* Note that "intensity bar" is inten80 in s1rcolor, not the full of s2color.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
intensity p        inten80

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Font sizes (Stata gsize keywords, relative units)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gsize text          medium
gsize heading       large
gsize axis_title    medsmall
gsize tick_label    medsmall
gsize note          small

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Graph dimensions, in inches (consumed by section 10 for figure proportions)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphsize x  5.5
graphsize y  4

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Default marker size for the p cycle
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
symbolsize p  medium

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Legend placement
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
clockdir legend_position  6
numstyle legend_cols      2

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Major grid switches, as Stata's s1rcolor declares them.  SchemeParser
* stores these in _props but _init_properties() exposes no attribute for
* them yet; recorded so the declared value is available when a consumer
* lands, and so the value is not lost from the translation.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* GRID VISIBILITY.  A Stata grid belongs to an AXIS and the key is named for
* that axis's orientation, not for the direction of the lines:
*   style/axisstyle-horizontal_default.style:18  draw_major_grid <- draw_major_hgrid
*   style/axisstyle-vertical_default.style:18    draw_major_grid <- draw_major_vgrid
* The horizontal axis is x, and its major grid lines are the VERTICAL ones at
* the x ticks; the vertical axis is y, and its lines are HORIZONTAL.
* `yesno draw_major_grid' below is transcribed faithfully from Stata's file but
* is DEAD at scheme level: grep "scheme draw_major_grid" over
* /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/style/ returns nothing.  dash used to read it
* for the y axis, which is why every scheme reported "no grid" and dash drew
* both anyway.
yesno draw_major_hgrid  no
yesno draw_major_vgrid no
yesno draw_major_grid   no

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Added 22sep2026 by scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py (WP-16): directives
* Stata consumes that the translation above did not carry.  Values are
* resolved from the same Stata #include chain and style files as the
* rest of this file (chain: s2color -> s1color -> s1rcolor); colours are
* pre-resolved #rrggbb.  Re-running the script re-checks every directive
* in this file and appends only what is missing.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Minor grid switches -- EFFECTIVE per-axis values.  twoway builds the x
* axis with `axisstyle horizontal_default' and the y axis with `axisstyle
* vertical_default'; the scheme maps each role to a style name, and that
* style file names the `yesno' key Stata actually reads:
*   x axis: axisstyle horizontal_default = horizontal_default
*           -> style/axisstyle-horizontal_default.style
*           -> draw_major_hgrid / draw_minor_hgrid
*   y axis: axisstyle vertical_default = vertical_default
*           -> style/axisstyle-vertical_default.style
*           -> draw_major_vgrid / draw_minor_vgrid
* The draw_major_hgrid / draw_major_vgrid lines above hold the same
* effective values.  `yesno draw_minor_grid' is transcribed from Stata's
* file but, like draw_major_grid, no style file reads it.
yesno draw_minor_hgrid  no
yesno draw_minor_vgrid  no
yesno draw_minor_grid   no

* Text colours, one per textbox style: style/textboxstyle-<name>.style
* reads `color <name>'.  title() is heading (above), subtitle()
* subheading, caption() body, note() small_body, legend keys key_label,
* axis titles axis_title, tick labels tick_label.  `color text' and
* `color foreground' are the scheme's general text and foreground
* colours.
color subheading  #ffffff
color body        #ffffff
color small_body  #ffffff
color text        #ffffff
color axis_title  #ffffff
color tick_label  #ffffff
color key_label   #ffffff
color foreground  #ffffff

* Text sizes, one per textbox style (Stata gsize style names; the
* fixture's _meta.units gives each name's relative value and its points
* at Stata's 4-inch reference).  note() is drawn with small_body: the
* `gsize note' line above is not the key Stata's note textbox reads.
gsize subheading  medium
gsize body        medsmall
gsize small_body  small
gsize key_label   medsmall

* Minor grid and axis line widths (Stata linewidth style names).
linewidth minor_grid  thin
linewidth axisline    thin

* Legend rows; 0 means not fixed, so the column count above decides.
numstyle legend_rows  0

